1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,650
Your phone didn't get old.

2
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:05,100
Maybe only its battery got tired.

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:09,300
Master, my phone freezes, the charge doesn't last till evening.

4
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:11,330
It's been two years, it's old.

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,940
I'll buy a new one on installments!

6
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:17,700
Diyor, who told you it freezes because it's old?

7
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:19,560
Everybody knows that!

8
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:22,560
Quiet, Diyor. Look.

9
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:28,220
Geneva, December 1924.

10
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:32,540
The world's biggest light bulb makers agreed:

11
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:37,240
an ordinary bulb must not burn more than a thousand hours.

12
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:41,220
Before that, bulbs burned up to 2,500 hours.

13
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:44,560
A factory whose bulbs lasted longer paid a fine.

14
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:46,790
On purpose?!

15
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:49,890
2017.

16
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:55,920
One of the most famous phone companies admitted a secret.

17
00:00:56,190 --> 00:00:57,270
What secret?

18
00:00:57,750 --> 00:01:01,790
It slowed down phones with worn-out batteries.

19
00:01:02,470 --> 00:01:04,250
So they wouldn't suddenly shut down.

20
00:01:04,850 --> 00:01:06,490
But it didn't tell the owners.

21
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:10,770
People said “my phone is old” and bought a new one.

22
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:14,420
Often, just replacing the battery was enough.

23
00:01:14,910 --> 00:01:20,160
When it came out, the company agreed to pay people in the US up to half a billion dollars.

24
00:01:20,710 --> 00:01:23,640
In France it was fined 25 million euros.

25
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:26,700
So my phone isn't old either,

26
00:01:27,050 --> 00:01:29,580
maybe just its battery is tired?

27
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:31,470
Maybe.

28
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:36,650
Forgive me, old friend... it wasn't your fault!

29
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:39,420
Don't hug it, check its battery!

30
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:42,450
Three checks before you buy a new one.

31
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:44,950
What's the battery health?

32
00:01:45,630 --> 00:01:47,140
Is the storage full?

33
00:01:47,860 --> 00:01:49,880
How much does a new battery cost?

34
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:54,570
They sell you not a phone, but the feeling that you got old.

35
00:01:55,170 --> 00:01:57,850
Always ask: who profits from this?

36
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:02,040
Is your phone freezing? Send its model to our bot:

37
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:03,900
@sahiychishopbot

38
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:07,470
It shows you where to find the battery health

39
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:11,040
and what to check before buying a new one.

